# Quality gate (mandatory)

This project uses **Agent Diff Gate** (`check_diff.py`). Before ANY commit:

1. Run: `python check_diff.py --staged`
2. If it exits non-zero, fix every finding and re-run until `GATE: PASS`.
3. Never commit with findings. Never use `git commit --no-verify`.

The gate flags hardcoded secrets, swallowed errors, missing error handling,
duplicate logic, ignored existing patterns, unsafe execution, SQL injection
and more — see `python check_diff.py --list-rules`.

## Log before you fix

Found an error? Log it first, then fix:

```sh
python check_diff.py --add --area "<what broke>" \
  --error "<symptom>" --cause "<root cause>"
```

and reference it in the commit message: `fix <thing> (AREA: <what broke>)`.
